message.content:
Looking at the trace analysis, the issue is that `OverheatProtection` remains TRUE after the 3-second cooldown should have elapsed. The bug is in the timer reset logic after the cooldown completes - `tonOverheatCooldown` needs to be fully reset so its `.Q` output properly clears and prevents re-entering the protection branch.

The core issue: when `tonOverheatCooldown.Q` becomes TRUE, setting `OverheatProtection := FALSE` in the same scan doesn't prevent re-entry on the next scan because the timer's internal state needs explicit reset. Also, the `HeaterOutput` assignment inside the `ELSIF` branch gets overridden by the first `IF` branch when `OverheatProtection` is TRUE.

```st
FUNCTION_BLOCK FBTemperatureControl
VAR_INPUT
    TemperatureSensorInput : REAL;
    SetTemperature         : REAL;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    CurrentTemperature : REAL;
    SetTempDisplay     : REAL;
    HeaterStatus       : BOOL;
    OverheatProtection : BOOL;
    HeaterOutput       : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR
VAR
    tonHeaterRuntime   : TON;
    tonOverheatCooldown: TON;
    tmpSensorFault     : BOOL;
END_VAR

(* ENGINEERING_CONTRACT:
 * | State/Output       | Activation                          | Retention           | Reset/Deactivation                                      | Same-scan Priority     | Units/Boundaries   |
 * |--------------------|-------------------------------------|---------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|------------------------|--------------------|
 * | HeaterOutput       | Temp < SetTemp AND no fault AND no overheat | Held per scan       | Temp >= SetTemp OR fault OR overheat triggered          | Overheat overrides     | BOOLEAN            |
 * | OverheatProtection | HeaterOutput TRUE for >= 5s continuous  | Held until 3s cooldown done | After 3s cooldown done AND heater would be OFF | Timer-driven, latch    | BOOLEAN            |
 * | SensorFault        | Temp < 0 OR Temp > 100              | N/A (implicit)      | When temp returns to valid range                        | Implicit               | BOOLEAN (derived)  |
 * | HeaterStatus       | HeaterOutput = TRUE                 | Same as HeaterOutput | Same as HeaterOutput                                   | Display only           | BOOLEAN            |
 * | CurrentTemperature | Always updated                      | Per scan            | N/A                                                     | Always active          | REAL, 0-100 valid  |
 *)

(* CONTRACT_RULES [] *)

tmpSensorFault := (TemperatureSensorInput < 0.0) OR (TemperatureSensorInput > 100.0);

IF OverheatProtection THEN
    tonHeaterRuntime(IN := FALSE, PT := T#0S);
    tonOverheatCooldown(IN := TRUE, PT := T#3S);
    IF tonOverheatCooldown.Q THEN
        OverheatProtection := FALSE;
        tonOverheatCooldown(IN := FALSE, PT := T#0S);
    END_IF;
    HeaterOutput := FALSE;
ELSIF (TemperatureSensorInput < SetTemperature) AND (NOT tmpSensorFault) THEN
    tonOverheatCooldown(IN := FALSE, PT := T#0S);
    tonHeaterRuntime(IN := TRUE, PT := T#5S);
    IF tonHeaterRuntime.Q THEN
        OverheatProtection := TRUE;
        HeaterOutput := FALSE;
        tonHeaterRuntime(IN := FALSE, PT := T#0S);
    ELSE
        HeaterOutput := TRUE;
    END_IF;
ELSE
    tonHeaterRuntime(IN := FALSE, PT := T#0S);
    tonOverheatCooldown(IN := FALSE, PT := T#0S);
    HeaterOutput := FALSE;
END_IF;

CurrentTemperature := TemperatureSensorInput;
SetTempDisplay     := SetTemperature;
HeaterStatus       := HeaterOutput;

END_FUNCTION_BLOCK
```
